From 12d643cf97a685750a366c4a3e5c9319a39c6c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(disk-cleanup): serialize tracked.json writers; unique
 temp file [daveey]

Parallel tool calls and every Hermes process on a host share
disk-cleanup/tracked.json. save_tracked always wrote the fixed name
tracked.json.tmp then replace()d it, and track()/forget()/quick() did
read-change-write with no lock, so concurrent writers renamed each
other's temp away (FileNotFoundError out of post_tool_call) and dropped
entries (4 procs x 150 track(): 403 errors, 19/600 kept).

- _tracked_lock(): process RLock + flock on disk-cleanup/tracked.lock,
  re-entrant per thread, around every read-change-write.
- save_tracked writes via utils.atomic_json_write (unique temp + fsync),
  still keeps .bak.
- quick() holds the lock for its tracked-state pass only; the empty-dir
  sweep runs outside it.
- post_tool_call catches track failures and writes 'ERROR: track failed'
  to cleanup.log instead of raising.

Self-heal plugin-129c2f2518.
